/-!
# Hubbard 2006, Chapter 3 §3.9: Fundamental domains

Source: Hubbard, *Teichmüller Theory*, Vol. 1, `H1` lines 2713–3085.

**Conventions.** Fuchsian groups are subgroups of `SL(2, ℝ)` acting on `ℍ` (`ℍ ≅ 𝔻`); orbit statements are read in `ℍ`.
*Fundamental domain* (Def. 3.9.1) is `IsFundamentalDomainTop`: a set `U` meeting every orbit at most once, whose closure
meets every orbit. (`LiZhongQC.IsFundamentalDomainH` is a measurable, a.e. notion on `ℍ` and is not the same
definition.) *Paired polygon* (Def. 3.9.2): the raw data `PolygonData` — a closed convex polygon `P ⊆ ℍ` with locally
finitely many sides, sides `s i`, `s' i` labelled by `I`, and pairing elements `g i` — and the conditions
`IsPairedPolygon`. The surface `X = P/∼` is `polyQuot` (quotient topology, `∼` generated by `x ∼ g_i x` for `x ∈ s_i`),
with the quotient metric `polygonQuotientDist` (the infimum of the sums of distances along chains through the pairing).
The angle `α_x(P)` at a vertex is the angle between the two sides through it (`IsVertexAngle`; `Katok1992.hypAngle`,
which is `π` for collinear sides) and the vertices are the points on two distinct sides. *Part 2* of the Poincaré
